    regenlmeta:photoCaptionStatus "candidate-visual-and-license-review-needed" ;
    regenlmeta:photoPracticeDescription "The photograph shows milk being processed into cheese on a farm. It illustrates adding value through on-farm processing as an aspect of the practice “Income deepening -increasing added value of product”."@en,
        "De foto toont het verwerken van melk tot kaas op een boerderij. Zo wordt het toevoegen van waarde door verwerking op het bedrijf zichtbaar als onderdeel van de praktijk ‘Inkomensverdieping door hogere productwaarde’."@nl .

vocab:NonChemicalControlWeedsPestsAndDiseases a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:source <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TractorWithMountedRototiller.JPG> ;
    skos:altLabel "Non-chemical control- weeds, pests and diseases"@en ;
    skos:broader vocab:PlantProtection ;
    skos:changeNote "Definitie en overgenomen uit ReGeNL practice_list_0.2.1, kolom: English scientific. Bronbestand: practice_list_0.2.1__git_ (1).xlsx."@nl ;
    skos:definition "Controlling weeds, pests and crop diseases with mechanical, physical, biological or cultural methods instead of chemical pesticides."@en,
        "Het beheersen van onkruid, plagen en gewasziekten met mechanische, fysieke, biologische of teeltkundige methoden in plaats van chemische middelen."@nl ;
    skos:editorialNote "Bilingual definition drafted for the PoC; requires validation by ReGeNL domain experts. Previous source definitions are retained in regenlmeta:originalDefinition."@en ;
    skos:historyNote "Voorgaande PoC-definitie (en): A ClassificationElement in the RegenerativePracticeFramework at Meso level with label 'Non-chemical control- weeds, pests and diseases'."@nl,
        "Voorgaande PoC-definitie (en): integrated pest management means careful consideration of all available plant protection methods and subsequent integration of appropriate measures that discourage the development of populations of harmful organisms and keep the use of plant protection products and other forms of intervention to levels that are economically and ecologically justified and reduce or minimise risks to human health and the environment"@nl ;
    skos:inScheme vocab: ;
    skos:narrower vocab:AlternativeBiocontrolProductUse,
        vocab:IntegratedPestManagementPrinciplesIPM,
        vocab:IntegratedWeedManagement,
        vocab:MechanicalPestManagement,
        vocab:MechanicalWeedManagement,
        vocab:NaturalPestManagement,
        vocab:NaturalWeedManagement ;
    skos:notation "Meso" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Non-chemical  control- weeds, pests and diseases"@en,
        "Niet-chemische beheersing van onkruid, plagen en ziekten"@nl ;
    foaf:depiction <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/file/TractorWithMountedRototiller.JPG?width=960> ;
    regenlmeta:definitionStatus "editorial-draft" ;
    regenlmeta:originalDefinition "integrated pest management means careful consideration of all available plant protection methods and subsequent integration of appropriate measures that discourage the development of populations of harmful organisms and keep the use of plant protection products and other forms of intervention to levels that are economically and ecologically justified and reduce or minimise risks to human health and the environment"@en ;
    regenlmeta:photoCaptionStatus "candidate-visual-and-license-review-needed" ;
    regenlmeta:photoPracticeDescription "The photograph shows an agricultural subject identified in the source as “TractorWithMountedRototiller”. It illustrates the related agricultural context as an aspect of the practice “Non-chemical  control- weeds, pests and diseases”."@en,
        "De foto toont een landbouwkundig onderwerp dat in de bron als ‘TractorWithMountedRototiller’ wordt aangeduid. Zo wordt de betreffende landbouwcontext zichtbaar als onderdeel van de praktijk ‘Niet-chemische beheersing van onkruid, plagen en ziekten’."@nl .

vocab:TreePlanning a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:source <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hedgerow_planting_on_footpath_near_Witley_Farm_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2859786.jpg> ;
    skos:broader vocab:AgroforestryAndPerennialIntegratedSystems ;
    skos:definition "Planning where and how trees will be planted and managed on a farm, including species choice, spacing, maintenance and intended functions."@en,
        "Het plannen waar en hoe bomen op een landbouwbedrijf worden aangeplant en beheerd, inclusief soortkeuze, plantafstand, onderhoud en beoogde functies."@nl ;
